{"title": "RF Energy Harvesting & Adaptive PMU | Berkay Özbek", "children": [{"tag": "section", "attrs": {"class": "project-hero container"}, "children": [{"tag": "a", "attrs": {"class": "back", "href": "/#research"}, "children": ["← Research portfolio"]}, {"tag": "p", "attrs": {"class": "eyebrow"}, "children": ["PHD RESEARCH / RF ENERGY HARVESTING"]}, {"tag": "h1", "attrs": {}, "children": ["RF energy harvesting & adaptive power management."]}, {"tag": "p", "attrs": {"class": "lead"}, "children": ["RF rectification and power management that adapt to changing coupling, from weak-input turn-on to efficient regulation under stronger RF drive."]}, {"tag": "div", "attrs": {"class": "project-meta"}, "children": [{"tag": "span", "attrs": {}, "children": ["180 nm & 65 nm silicon"]}, {"tag": "span", "attrs": {}, "children": ["Measured at 433 MHz"]}, {"tag": "span", "attrs": {}, "children": ["CICC 2026 · BioCAS 2024"]}]}, {"tag": "div", "attrs": {"class": "actions"}, "children": [{"tag": "a", "attrs": {"class": "text-link", "href": "https://doi.org/10.1109/CICC65509.2026.11509465", "target": "_blank", "rel": "noopener"}, "children": ["CICC paper ", {"tag": "span", "attrs": {"aria-hidden": "true"}, "children": ["↗"]}]}, {"tag": "a", "attrs": {"class": "text-link", "href": "/documents/Berkay_Ozbek_PhD_Thesis.pdf#page=117", "target": "_blank", "rel": "noopener"}, "children": ["Thesis chapter 4 ", {"tag": "span", "attrs": {"aria-hidden": "true"}, "children": ["↗"]}]}]}]}, {"tag": "div", "attrs": {"class": "container project-content"}, "children": [{"tag": "div", "attrs": {"class": "metric-band"}, "children": [{"tag": "div", "attrs": {"class": "metric"}, "children": [{"tag": "strong", "attrs": {}, "children": ["91.5%"]}, {"tag": "span", "attrs": {}, "children": ["Peak rectifier-core PCE"]}, {"tag": "small", "attrs": {}, "children": ["65 nm · 100 kΩ · 433 MHz"]}]}, {"tag": "div", "attrs": {"class": "metric"}, "children": [{"tag": "strong", "attrs": {}, "children": ["85.12%"]}, {"tag": "span", "attrs": {}, "children": ["Peak RF–DC chain efficiency"]}, {"tag": "small", "attrs": {}, "children": ["Matching & regulation enabled"]}]}, {"tag": "div", "attrs": {"class": "metric"}, "children": [{"tag": "strong", "attrs": {}, "children": ["32.48 dB"]}, {"tag": "span", "attrs": {}, "children": ["Power-chain dynamic range"]}, {"tag": "small", "attrs": {}, "children": ["Efficiency above 20%"]}]}]}, {"tag": "div", "attrs": {"class": "story-intro"}, "children": [{"tag": "h2", "attrs": {}, "children": ["Low-power turn-on and reverse-current suppression"]}, {"tag": "div", "attrs": {}, "children": [{"tag": "p", "attrs": {}, "children": ["A passive rectifier must conduct at weak RF inputs without losing that benefit to reverse current when the received power rises. My ULP-assisted architecture uses two complementary paths to address these operating regions."]}, {"tag": "p", "attrs": {}, "children": ["An RF-driven feedforward path assists low-power turn-on. A feedback path derived from the rectified output suppresses reverse conduction as the output rises. Their different RF/DC behaviour allows the two functions to be designed together."]}]}]}, {"tag": "figure", "attrs": {"class": "research-figure "}, "children": [{"tag": "a", "attrs": {"href": "/assets/rectifier-concept.webp", "class": "figure-open", "data-caption": "Dual-path ULP-assisted rectification", "aria-label": "Enlarge figure: Dual-path ULP-assisted rectification"}, "children": [{"tag": "img", "attrs": {"class": "", "src": "/assets/rectifier-concept.webp", "width": "2200", "height": "1040", "alt": "Dual-path ULP-assisted rectification", "loading": "lazy", "decoding": "async"}, "children": []}, {"tag": "span", "attrs": {"class": "enlarge"}, "children": ["Enlarge ↗"]}]}, {"tag": "figcaption", "attrs": {}, "children": [{"tag": "strong", "attrs": {}, "children": ["Dual-path ULP-assisted rectification"]}, {"tag": "p", "attrs": {}, "children": ["The original circuit concept contrasts the conventional cross-coupled core with RF feedforward assistance and output-derived reverse blocking."]}, {"tag": "a", "attrs": {"class": "source", "href": "/documents/Berkay_Ozbek_PhD_Thesis.pdf#page=124", "target": "_blank", "rel": "noopener"}, "children": ["PhD thesis · Fig. 4.2 · p. 108 ", {"tag": "span", "attrs": {"aria-hidden": "true"}, "children": ["↗"]}]}]}]}, "\n", {"tag": "section", "attrs": {"class": "content-section"}, "children": [{"tag": "p", "attrs": {"class": "eyebrow"}, "children": ["RECTIFIER-CORE MEASUREMENTS"]}, {"tag": "h2", "attrs": {}, "children": ["Rectifier measurements in 180 nm and 65 nm"]}, {"tag": "figure", "attrs": {"class": "research-figure "}, "children": [{"tag": "a", "attrs": {"href": "/assets/rectifier-180.webp", "class": "figure-open", "data-caption": "A co-fabricated 180-nm comparison", "aria-label": "Enlarge figure: A co-fabricated 180-nm comparison"}, "children": [{"tag": "img", "attrs": {"class": "", "src": "/assets/rectifier-180.webp", "width": "2200", "height": "791", "alt": "A co-fabricated 180-nm comparison", "loading": "lazy", "decoding": "async"}, "children": []}, {"tag": "span", "attrs": {"class": "enlarge"}, "children": ["Enlarge ↗"]}]}, {"tag": "figcaption", "attrs": {}, "children": [{"tag": "strong", "attrs": {}, "children": ["A co-fabricated 180-nm comparison"]}, {"tag": "p", "attrs": {}, "children": ["All three cores were measured at 433 MHz with a 100 kΩ load after RF-feed and matching-network de-embedding, providing a controlled architectural comparison."]}, {"tag": "a", "attrs": {"class": "source", "href": "/documents/Berkay_Ozbek_PhD_Thesis.pdf#page=144", "target": "_blank", "rel": "noopener"}, "children": ["PhD thesis · Fig. 4.7 · p. 128 ", {"tag": "span", "attrs": {"aria-hidden": "true"}, "children": ["↗"]}]}]}]}, "\n", {"tag": "div", "attrs": {"class": "table-wrap", "tabindex": "0", "role": "region", "aria-label": "180-nm rectifier benchmark under common conditions"}, "children": [{"tag": "table", "attrs": {}, "children": [{"tag": "caption", "attrs": {}, "children": ["180-nm rectifier benchmark under common conditions"]}, {"tag": "thead", "attrs": {}, "children": [{"tag": "tr", "attrs": {}, "children": [{"tag": "th", "attrs": {"scope": "col"}, "children": ["Core"]}, {"tag": "th", "attrs": {"scope": "col"}, "children": ["Peak PCE"]}, {"tag": "th", "attrs": {"scope": "col"}, "children": ["Sensitivity at 1 V output"]}]}]}, {"tag": "tbody", "attrs": {}, "children": [{"tag": "tr", "attrs": {}, "children": [{"tag": "th", "attrs": {"scope": "row"}, "children": ["Conventional cross-coupled"]}, {"tag": "td", "attrs": {}, "children": ["77.1%"]}, {"tag": "td", "attrs": {}, "children": ["−13.9 dBm"]}]}, {"tag": "tr", "attrs": {}, "children": [{"tag": "th", "attrs": {"scope": "row"}, "children": ["Double-sided reference"]}, {"tag": "td", "attrs": {}, "children": ["64.5%"]}, {"tag": "td", "attrs": {}, "children": ["−17.9 dBm"]}]}, {"tag": "tr", "attrs": {}, "children": [{"tag": "th", "attrs": {"scope": "row"}, "children": ["Proposed ULP-assisted"]}, {"tag": "td", "attrs": {}, "children": ["90.1%"]}, {"tag": "td", "attrs": {}, "children": ["−19.45 dBm"]}]}]}]}]}, {"tag": "p", "attrs": {"class": "table-note"}, "children": ["100 kΩ load, 433 MHz, de-embedded measurements. The proposed core achieves a 29.13 dB dynamic range at PCE > 20%. Source: PhD thesis Fig. 4.7 and §4.6.2."]}, {"tag": "figure", "attrs": {"class": "research-figure "}, "children": [{"tag": "a", "attrs": {"href": "/assets/rectifier-65.webp", "class": "figure-open", "data-caption": "Five dies, three loads, one 65-nm architecture", "aria-label": "Enlarge figure: Five dies, three loads, one 65-nm architecture"}, "children": [{"tag": "img", "attrs": {"class": "", "src": "/assets/rectifier-65.webp", "width": "2200", "height": "768", "alt": "Five dies, three loads, one 65-nm architecture", "loading": "lazy", "decoding": "async"}, "children": []}, {"tag": "span", "attrs": {"class": "enlarge"}, "children": ["Enlarge ↗"]}]}, {"tag": "figcaption", "attrs": {}, "children": [{"tag": "strong", "attrs": {}, "children": ["Five dies, three loads, one 65-nm architecture"]}, {"tag": "p", "attrs": {}, "children": ["Across five dies, peak PCE at 100 kΩ ranges from 86.7% to 91.5%. At 1 MΩ, the measured 1-V sensitivity ranges from −25.36 to −25.22 dBm. These peak-efficiency and best-sensitivity results occur under different loads."]}, {"tag": "a", "attrs": {"class": "source", "href": "/documents/Berkay_Ozbek_PhD_Thesis.pdf#page=145", "target": "_blank", "rel": "noopener"}, "children": ["PhD thesis · Fig. 4.8 · p. 129 ", {"tag": "span", "attrs": {"aria-hidden": "true"}, "children": ["↗"]}]}]}]}, {"tag": "div", "attrs": {"class": "table-wrap", "tabindex": "0", "role": "region", "aria-label": "65-nm rectifier results by load"}, "children": [{"tag": "table", "attrs": {}, "children": [{"tag": "caption", "attrs": {}, "children": ["65-nm rectifier results by load"]}, {"tag": "thead", "attrs": {}, "children": [{"tag": "tr", "attrs": {}, "children": [{"tag": "th", "attrs": {"scope": "col"}, "children": ["Load"]}, {"tag": "th", "attrs": {"scope": "col"}, "children": ["Peak PCE across five dies"]}, {"tag": "th", "attrs": {"scope": "col"}, "children": ["Sensitivity across five dies"]}]}]}, {"tag": "tbody", "attrs": {}, "children": [{"tag": "tr", "attrs": {}, "children": [{"tag": "th", "attrs": {"scope": "row"}, "children": ["3 kΩ"]}, {"tag": "td", "attrs": {}, "children": ["80.7–88.7%"]}, {"tag": "td", "attrs": {}, "children": ["−3.57 to −3.26 dBm"]}]}, {"tag": "tr", "attrs": {}, "children": [{"tag": "th", "attrs": {"scope": "row"}, "children": ["100 kΩ"]}, {"tag": "td", "attrs": {}, "children": ["86.7–91.5%"]}, {"tag": "td", "attrs": {}, "children": ["−18.90 to −18.61 dBm"]}]}, {"tag": "tr", "attrs": {}, "children": [{"tag": "th", "attrs": {"scope": "row"}, "children": ["1 MΩ"]}, {"tag": "td", "attrs": {}, "children": ["46.0–48.7%"]}, {"tag": "td", "attrs": {}, "children": ["−25.36 to −25.22 dBm"]}]}]}]}]}, {"tag": "p", "attrs": {"class": "table-note"}, "children": ["Sensitivity: 1 V output criterion. All measurements at 433 MHz. At 100 kΩ, PDR = 24.196 dB (approximately 24.2 dB), defined at PCE > 20%. Source: PhD thesis Fig. 4.8."]}]}, {"tag": "section", "attrs": {"class": "content-section"}, "children": [{"tag": "p", "attrs": {"class": "eyebrow"}, "children": ["ABSOLUTE-PEAK TUNING & SELF-REGULATION"]}, {"tag": "h2", "attrs": {}, "children": ["Joint impedance tuning and rectifier regulation"]}, {"tag": "p", "attrs": {"class": "prose"}, "children": ["A high rectifier output can still waste energy in the regulator. The PMU therefore coordinates impedance matching with rectifier mode selection to keep the rectified voltage close to the headroom needed by the regulated rail."]}, {"tag": "figure", "attrs": {"class": "research-figure "}, "children": [{"tag": "a", "attrs": {"href": "/assets/pmu-architecture.webp", "class": "figure-open", "data-caption": "A two-pass search, repeated after mode selection", "aria-label": "Enlarge figure: A two-pass search, repeated after mode selection"}, "children": [{"tag": "img", "attrs": {"class": "", "src": "/assets/pmu-architecture.webp", "width": "2200", "height": "1358", "alt": "A two-pass search, repeated after mode selection", "loading": "lazy", "decoding": "async"}, "children": []}, {"tag": "span", "attrs": {"class": "enlarge"}, "children": ["Enlarge ↗"]}]}, {"tag": "figcaption", "attrs": {}, "children": [{"tag": "strong", "attrs": {}, "children": ["A two-pass search, repeated after mode selection"]}, {"tag": "p", "attrs": {}, "children": ["An auxiliary rectifier supplies a power proxy. The first pass stores the largest response; a second pass recovers the corresponding matching code using a controlled decay margin. A mode change triggers another search because it changes the rectifier’s RF input impedance."]}, {"tag": "a", "attrs": {"class": "source", "href": "/documents/Berkay_Ozbek_PhD_Thesis.pdf#page=129", "target": "_blank", "rel": "noopener"}, "children": ["PhD thesis · Fig. 4.3 · p. 113 ", {"tag": "span", "attrs": {"aria-hidden": "true"}, "children": ["↗"]}]}]}]}, "\n", {"tag": "div", "attrs": {"class": "three-col principles"}, "children": [{"tag": "article", "attrs": {}, "children": [{"tag": "span", "attrs": {}, "children": ["01 / ACQUIRE"]}, {"tag": "h3", "attrs": {}, "children": ["Acquire the maximum response"]}, {"tag": "p", "attrs": {}, "children": ["Sweep the discrete matching candidates and retain the largest auxiliary response in an analog peak-hold node."]}]}, {"tag": "article", "attrs": {}, "children": [{"tag": "span", "attrs": {}, "children": ["02 / RECONFIGURE"]}, {"tag": "h3", "attrs": {}, "children": ["Select the rectifier mode"]}, {"tag": "p", "attrs": {}, "children": ["Select among Low4×, Low2×, High2× and High1× to balance sensitivity, reverse blocking and regulator headroom."]}]}, {"tag": "article", "attrs": {}, "children": [{"tag": "span", "attrs": {}, "children": ["03 / HOLD"]}, {"tag": "h3", "attrs": {}, "children": ["Retune and enter steady state"]}, {"tag": "p", "attrs": {}, "children": ["Repeat the matching search for the selected mode, latch the final settings and disable the search clock in steady state."]}]}]}, "\n", {"tag": "figure", "attrs": {"class": "research-figure "}, "children": [{"tag": "a", "attrs": {"href": "/assets/regulated-power.webp", "class": "figure-open", "data-caption": "Measured self-regulated rectification", "aria-label": "Enlarge figure: Measured self-regulated rectification"}, "children": [{"tag": "img", "attrs": {"class": "", "src": "/assets/regulated-power.webp", "width": "2200", "height": "726", "alt": "Measured self-regulated rectification", "loading": "lazy", "decoding": "async"}, "children": []}, {"tag": "span", "attrs": {"class": "enlarge"}, "children": ["Enlarge ↗"]}]}, {"tag": "figcaption", "attrs": {}, "children": [{"tag": "strong", "attrs": {}, "children": ["Measured self-regulated rectification"]}, {"tag": "p", "attrs": {}, "children": ["The 65-nm measurements at 433 MHz and 3 kΩ show autonomous mode changes and control of the rectified voltage relative to the 1.2 V rail."]}, {"tag": "a", "attrs": {"class": "source", "href": "/documents/Berkay_Ozbek_PhD_Thesis.pdf#page=146", "target": "_blank", "rel": "noopener"}, "children": ["PhD thesis · Fig. 4.9 · p. 130 ", {"tag": "span", "attrs": {"aria-hidden": "true"}, "children": ["↗"]}]}]}]}, "\n", {"tag": "div", "attrs": {"class": "figure-pair"}, "children": [{"tag": "figure", "attrs": {"class": "research-figure "}, "children": [{"tag": "a", "attrs": {"href": "/assets/absolute-peak.webp", "class": "figure-open", "data-caption": "Finding the largest tested response", "aria-label": "Enlarge figure: Finding the largest tested response"}, "children": [{"tag": "img", "attrs": {"class": "", "src": "/assets/absolute-peak.webp", "width": "2082", "height": "772", "alt": "Finding the largest tested response", "loading": "lazy", "decoding": "async"}, "children": []}, {"tag": "span", "attrs": {"class": "enlarge"}, "children": ["Enlarge ↗"]}]}, {"tag": "figcaption", "attrs": {}, "children": [{"tag": "strong", "attrs": {}, "children": ["Finding the largest tested response"]}, {"tag": "p", "attrs": {}, "children": ["Measured multi-peak input demonstrates selection of the global maximum within the tested candidate set. Reliable discrimination depends on peak separation, settling and comparator/hold-node uncertainty."]}, {"tag": "a", "attrs": {"class": "source", "href": "/documents/Berkay_Ozbek_PhD_Thesis.pdf#page=147", "target": "_blank", "rel": "noopener"}, "children": ["PhD thesis · Fig. 4.10 · p. 131 ", {"tag": "span", "attrs": {"aria-hidden": "true"}, "children": ["↗"]}]}]}]}, {"tag": "figure", "attrs": {"class": "research-figure "}, "children": [{"tag": "a", "attrs": {"href": "/assets/cold-start.webp", "class": "figure-open", "data-caption": "From cold start to steady state", "aria-label": "Enlarge figure: From cold start to steady state"}, "children": [{"tag": "img", "attrs": {"class": "", "src": "/assets/cold-start.webp", "width": "2200", "height": "2094", "alt": "From cold start to steady state", "loading": "lazy", "decoding": "async"}, "children": []}, {"tag": "span", "attrs": {"class": "enlarge"}, "children": ["Enlarge ↗"]}]}, {"tag": "figcaption", "attrs": {}, "children": [{"tag": "strong", "attrs": {}, "children": ["From cold start to steady state"]}, {"tag": "p", "attrs": {}, "children": ["Measured acquisition performs an initial search, updates the rectifier mode, retunes the matching network and then stops the supervisory clock."]}, {"tag": "a", "attrs": {"class": "source", "href": "/documents/Berkay_Ozbek_PhD_Thesis.pdf#page=148", "target": "_blank", "rel": "noopener"}, "children": ["PhD thesis · Fig. 4.11 · p. 132 ", {"tag": "span", "attrs": {"aria-hidden": "true"}, "children": ["↗"]}]}]}]}]}]}, "\n", {"tag": "section", "attrs": {"class": "content-section"}, "children": [{"tag": "p", "attrs": {"class": "eyebrow"}, "children": ["EX VIVO FUNCTIONAL VALIDATION"]}, {"tag": "h2", "attrs": {}, "children": ["Ex vivo PMU validation through tissue"]}, {"tag": "p", "attrs": {"class": "prose"}, "children": ["An additional experiment tested the PMU through an approximately 14.01 mm beef–bone medium, with tissue also behind the receiver. The fabricated system completed cold start, matching, mode selection and regulated-rail establishment under this more demanding loading condition."]}, {"tag": "div", "attrs": {"class": "figure-pair"}, "children": [{"tag": "figure", "attrs": {"class": "research-figure "}, "children": [{"tag": "a", "attrs": {"href": "/assets/tissue-setup.webp", "class": "figure-open", "data-caption": "Tissue-loaded proof-of-concept setup", "aria-label": "Enlarge figure: Tissue-loaded proof-of-concept setup"}, "children": [{"tag": "img", "attrs": {"class": "", "src": "/assets/tissue-setup.webp", "width": "1984", "height": "1600", "alt": "Tissue-loaded proof-of-concept setup", "loading": "lazy", "decoding": "async"}, "children": []}, {"tag": "span", "attrs": {"class": "enlarge"}, "children": ["Enlarge ↗"]}]}, {"tag": "figcaption", "attrs": {}, "children": [{"tag": "strong", "attrs": {}, "children": ["Tissue-loaded proof-of-concept setup"]}, {"tag": "p", "attrs": {}, "children": ["The available coil pair operated near 463 MHz. This experiment tests PMU functionality through the medium; it does not establish implant-scale link efficiency or in vivo performance."]}, {"tag": "a", "attrs": {"class": "source", "href": "/documents/Berkay_Ozbek_PhD_Thesis.pdf#page=150", "target": "_blank", "rel": "noopener"}, "children": ["PhD thesis · Fig. 4.14 · p. 134 ", {"tag": "span", "attrs": {"aria-hidden": "true"}, "children": ["↗"]}]}]}]}, {"tag": "figure", "attrs": {"class": "research-figure "}, "children": [{"tag": "a", "attrs": {"href": "/assets/tissue-rails.webp", "class": "figure-open", "data-caption": "Supply rails through the biological medium", "aria-label": "Enlarge figure: Supply rails through the biological medium"}, "children": [{"tag": "img", "attrs": {"class": "", "src": "/assets/tissue-rails.webp", "width": "2200", "height": "1580", "alt": "Supply rails through the biological medium", "loading": "lazy", "decoding": "async"}, "children": []}, {"tag": "span", "attrs": {"class": "enlarge"}, "children": ["Enlarge ↗"]}]}, {"tag": "figcaption", "attrs": {}, "children": [{"tag": "strong", "attrs": {}, "children": ["Supply rails through the biological medium"]}, {"tag": "p", "attrs": {}, "children": ["The clean 1.2 V core rail remains established while the auxiliary rails support impedance and rectifier reconfiguration."]}, {"tag": "a", "attrs": {"class": "source", "href": "/documents/Berkay_Ozbek_PhD_Thesis.pdf#page=152", "target": "_blank", "rel": "noopener"}, "children": ["PhD thesis · Fig. 4.16 · p. 136 ", {"tag": "span", "attrs": {"aria-hidden": "true"}, "children": ["↗"]}]}]}]}]}]}, "\n", {"tag": "aside", "attrs": {"class": "evidence-note"}, "children": [{"tag": "h3", "attrs": {}, "children": ["Measurement boundaries"]}, {"tag": "p", "attrs": {}, "children": ["The headline efficiency measurements use 433 MHz and stated electrical loads. The separate tissue-loaded functional experiment uses the available coils near 463 MHz. Its coil geometry and packaging were not optimised for a final implant. The excess-energy storage path did not consistently provide the intended reuse benefit; over-voltage protection and rectifier reconfiguration were the demonstrated protection mechanisms."]}]}, "\n", {"tag": "div", "attrs": {"class": "related"}, "children": [{"tag": "div", "attrs": {}, "children": [{"tag": "span", "attrs": {}, "children": ["RELATED RESEARCH"]}, {"tag": "h3", "attrs": {}, "children": ["See the integrated NeuroStreamX system"]}]}, {"tag": "a", "attrs": {"href": "/neurostreamx"}, "children": ["NeuroStreamX system ↗"]}]}]}]}